   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "lump/s or changes in skin colour? • Check for pregnancy 174. • Check for kidney disease on urine dipstick: if blood or protein, check BP 148 and refer to doctor. • If none of the above or unsure of diagnosis, refer same week.",
   "bbox": [
    373.3,
    381.0,
    785.3,
    511.2
   ],
   "key": "p80-6ea7a3a4"
  },
  {
   "id": "p80-out-e24",
   "page": 80,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Sprain/strain likely • Rest and elevate leg. • Apply ice and a pressure bandage. • Give ibuprofen2 400mg 8 hourly with/after food and paracetamol 500mg-1g 4-6 hourly (up to 4g in 24 hours) as needed for up to 5 days. • Advise to mobilise leg after 2-3 days, even if mild to moderate pain. • Refer for physiotherapy. • Review after 1 week: if no better, arrange x-ray and doctor review.",
   "bbox": [
    477.9,
    370.2,
    611.4,
    511.2
   ],
   "key": "p80-f2697575"
  },
