    765.0,
    442.1
   ],
   "key": "p80-137a4f98"
  },
  {
   "id": "p80-out-e27",
   "page": 80,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Irritation of sciatic nerve likely • Give paracetamol 500mg-1g 4-6 hourly (up to 4g in 24 hours) as needed for up to 5 days. • If no better, add ibuprofen2 400mg 8 hourly with/after food for up to 5 days. • Advise to be as active as possible, continue normal activity and avoid bed rest. • If available, refer for physiotherapy. • Explain that pain does not always mean a disease/cancer, and tests cannot always show a reason for the pain and often are not needed. • Advise to return and refer same day if: - Retention/incontinence of urine or stool - Numbness of buttocks/perineum/legs - Leg weakness - Difficulty walking. • If pain ≥ 3 months, assess 76 and refer to confirm diagnosis.",
   "bbox": [
    39.7,
    344.8,
    220.9,
    525.8
   ],
   "key": "p80-0632bacf"
